From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:21:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: honour FEX_HOSTFEATURES' AFP switch on the iOS host

The iOS branch of CPUFeatures::FetchHostFeatures builds the feature set
by hand and returns before FEX::FetchHostFeatures, so OverrideFeatures
never runs: FEX_HOSTFEATURES was read (the TSO config line prints it)
and ignored. With AFP, every x64 -> ARM64EC call and its return write
FPCR (ExitFunctionEC clears NEP/AH, the dispatcher sets them again),
and an FPCR write stalls Apple cores: in The Witcher 3 8.8 % of the
busiest threads' samples sit on ExitFunctionEC's msr FPCR. Honour
DISABLEAFP there and log the AFP state the JIT uses.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-witcher3-profile.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
index 3a61b45..4b21427 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 
 #include <FEXCore/Core/Context.h>
 #include <FEXCore/Core/HostFeatures.h>
+#include <FEXCore/Config/Config.h>
+#include <FEXCore/Utils/LogManager.h>
 #include <FEXCore/fextl/fmt.h>
 
 #include <windows.h>
@@ -74,6 +76,19 @@ FEXCore::HostFeatures CPUFeatures::FetchHostFeatures(bool IsWine, FEXCore::HostF
   HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM = true;
   HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM2 = true;
   HostFeatures.SupportsAFP = true;
+  {
+    /* Playport: the iOS branch returns before FEX::FetchHostFeatures, so
+     * OverrideFeatures never ran and FEX_HOSTFEATURES was read but ignored.
+     * Honour its AFP switch: with AFP, every x64 -> ARM64EC call and every
+     * return writes FPCR (ExitFunctionEC clears NEP/AH, the dispatcher sets
+     * them again), and an FPCR write stalls Apple cores. Without it, scalar
+     * SSE ops take a few more instructions and MXCSR.DAZ is not applied. */
+    FEX_CONFIG_OPT(HostFeatureControl, HOSTFEATURES);
+    if (HostFeatureControl() & FEXCore::Config::HostFeatures::DISABLEAFP) {
+      HostFeatures.SupportsAFP = false;
+    }
+    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: iOS host AFP={} (FEX_HOSTFEATURES={})", HostFeatures.SupportsAFP, HostFeatureControl());
+  }
   HostFeatures.CPUMIDRs.push_back(0u);
   HostFeatures.HostType = HostType;
   HostFeatures.ProcessPID = ProcessPID;
